description: Fenced code block. Open is a run of three or more backticks at line start; close is the same character with run length ≥ the open's, on its own line. Body is captured verbatim. First whitespace-delimited token of the info string becomes the `language-X` class on the inner `<code>` (CommonMark / GFM convention). The rest of the info string (when present) is parsed via TW's macro-parameter attribute parser and emitted as `data-*` attributes on the outer `<pre>` — MkDocs / Hugo / VuePress style: ` ```python title="src/auth.py" highlight=2,5 ` → `<pre data-title="src/auth.py" data-highlight="2,5">`. The `data-` prefix is the security boundary; any user-supplied attribute lands as an inert data attribute regardless of its name. Implicit close at EOF.
